## 🎯 **Premise Development Assignment – Awakened: Two Worlds, One Truth**

---

### ✅ 1. **Choose One of These Guiding Questions** (I'll answer all 3 for you to help you brainstorm):

#### ❓ *What is the main concept behind my story?*  
A spiritually blind society is unknowingly living in a controlled illusion until a forgotten truth begins to break through the system, sparking an internal and external rebellion.

#### ❓ *What message do I want to tell the world?*  
Truth cannot be fully erased — and even in a world built on lies, awakening is still possible when one person chooses to see.

#### ❓ *What statement am I trying to prove?*  
No matter how deeply truth is buried, it can still rise — and those who see it must risk everything to live by it.

---

### ✅ 2. **Answer All of the Following Based on Your Story:**

#### 🔹 *What is a trait of my main character that could lead to a premise?*  
Malak is observant, spiritually restless, and unwilling to accept surface-level answers — even when it puts him at risk.

#### 🔹 *What is the main conflict of my story?*  
Malak discovers that the world he serves is built on a false gospel, and he must decide whether to expose the truth or protect his life by staying silent.

#### 🔹 *What is the conclusion of my story?*  
Malak sacrifices his safety and possibly his life to awaken the world to truth. Though his fate is uncertain, his actions ignite a quiet spiritual rebellion in both cities.

---

### ✅ 3. **Write At Least One Possible Premise for Your Story:**

> **Premise:**  
When a spiritually starved technician glimpses a hidden truth in a world ruled by deception, his journey to expose it proves that awakening begins the moment one soul chooses truth over comfort — no matter the cost.

