### 💡 Why This Is the Right Answer:
This line is a classic example of **on-the-nose exposition** or **info-dumping** — the character tells us things they would never say to someone who already knows them. It’s clunky, unrealistic, and written just to deliver background to the audience. That’s a screenwriting red flag.

