In this assignment, you’ll turn your treatment from Week 3, into a formatted screenplay — taking yourself from storyteller to screenwriter. You do not need to write all 30 pages of the screenplay. Turning a treatment into a properly formatted screenplay is an essential step in the screenwriting process. A screenwriter must not only know storytelling, but also how to translate the words and structure of a treatment into a formatted screenplay that includes dialogue.

Instructions
Think about your story and treatment from Week 3. Choose a portion of the treatment to adapt into 3–4 scenes of a screenplay.
Remember that scenes will be separated by scene headings and take place at a different time/place form other scenes.

