### ✅ Example of How the Script Should Look (Excerpt)

```plaintext
INT. TRANSIT CORRIDOR – CONTINUOUS

A river of citizens moves with robotic precision — gray uniforms, blank faces, no eye contact.

MALAK (23), earbuds in, walks among them. His badge flashes:

                      SIGNAL RESTORATION – LEVEL 2

He looks up — just a flicker of doubt in his eyes.

EXT. SKYLINE OVERPASS – MOMENTS LATER

The crowd stops. Above them, a HOLO-BILLBOARD flashes scripture.

                        BILLBOARD (V.O.)
          “GOD HELPS THOSE WHO HELP THEMSELVES.”

The crowd chants in unison.

                        CROWD
          God helps those who help themselves.

Malak stares. His lips move, but doubt creeps in.

                        MALAK
          (softly)
          God helps those...

The screen glitches — a different verse flickers, almost too fast to see.

                        SCREEN (INSERT)
          “Blessed are the poor in spirit...” (Matt 5:3)
```

> Continue 2 more scenes to complete the 1–2 page total.

